(requirement (id "REQ-GC-C") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "The RV64+D C selection has 37 sixteen-bit forms, Zca plus Zcd. Each executes its declared single base-instruction expansion over the reconstructed compact registers and signed/scaled immediates; C.JALR takes its target from the old source and writes pc+2, including rd=rs1. Instruction PCs advance by two or four bytes under IALIGN=16. HINTs preserve architectural state except advancing PC and applicable performance counters, and C.EBREAK delivers breakpoint cause 3. Compressed D memory obeys the D extension and FS gate. Reserved operands are refused with their original sixteen bits under the declared illegal-instruction policy. Fetch reads the first parcel exactly and a second only for a 32-bit instruction; a second-parcel translation fault reports that parcel VA in xtval and the instruction start in xepc, before any instruction effect. The all-ones illegal instruction retains all ILEN=32 bits in the diagnostic. Valid C forms preserve the constrained LR/SC guarantee.") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.15")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status implemented) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The compressed forms expand as the chapter specifies; unmatched encodings use the separately declared illegal-instruction policy, and the environment's request extent is stated in OB-GC-ENV-FETCH-SUPPLY.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-GC-C"))
